    x86/mm/pti: Move user W+X check into pti_finalize()
    =

    The user page-table gets the updated kernel mappings in pti_finalize(),
    which runs after the RO+X permissions got applied to the kernel page-ta=
ble
    in mark_readonly().
    =

    But with CONFIG_DEBUG_WX enabled, the user page-table is already checke=
d in
    mark_readonly() for insecure mappings.  This causes false-positive
    warnings, because the user page-table did not get the updated mappings =
yet.
    =

    Move the W+X check for the user page-table into pti_finalize() after it
    updated all required mappings.
    =

